<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UK fighter jets to protect Saudi Arabia from Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36cf128f22a5d8ba99074cdc4881bb18666f3f30733491cdf380ac1f40eb5479</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T01:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467--d87226c03f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-fighter-jets-to-protect-saudi-arabia-from-houthi-attacks/a-79718467?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UK is sending military support to Saudi Arabia as Iran-aligned Houthi rebels launch repeated attacks on the kingdom.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal housing protests continue after police clear camps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2469f5bfb5fd1a45bb432a62a38a3900f622e88a411cb9a589c296eb38464da</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904--9c24875c39a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/portugal-housing-protests-continue-after-police-clear-camps/a-79717904?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators vow to continue their campaign to call for affordable housing in Portugal after police cleared tent camps and arrested at least 55 people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0d05cf40bd8550f0e48c300f51785eebb23998071eb5e7b3fe32802744f067a</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon faces uncertainty as UNIFIL mandate nears end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afad535eea7cdf8587737c419b0fc63445dffa736d9ab0b744431a6d095f2714</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491--a12453a4b744.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-faces-uncertainty-as-unifil-mandate-nears-end/a-79714491?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As UN peacekeeping forces prepare to withdraw from Lebanon, Israel remains present and Hezbollah is still armed. A new EU support mission aims to strengthen Lebanon's army, but will not replace UN peacekeepers.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan drone strike kills around 150 in Abyei market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1a0d6d178bb0971872af574059235646f91b7e013730c3b0688860828167854</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T18:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587--6d5e17c39f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drone-strike-kills-around-150-in-abyei-market/a-79716587?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone strike hit a market in the Abyei border region disputed by Sudan and South Sudan and killed dozens. The drone caused a large fire when it hit a fuel depot. South Sudanese officials blamed Sudan's military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4db01feb6420ae6a3c0a28088268ccf0f3b32a085fd637b1e3e1eb96a448ad3</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Flavio Bolsonaro tied ahead of runoff vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305538cfe9db421c40dc76da29c6741d7e9697ccdc42192cf139793fe38d7dc5</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182--cfbbc055c58e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-lula-flavio-bolsonaro-tied-ahead-of-runoff-vote/a-79715182?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With just under a week to go before the decisive presidential runoff election, polls show left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro are virtually tied.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fbc558b536d901dfdc4f151359d2fc3a0cf3eca217bae80ceb67e50de0fff7</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:044776afd8848d869644602bd285d4ab295db679b446668d357b5c93e6162bf1</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta rejects separation bid, CBC projects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fdd6c760bdbc465dfe6ae377b0ec541a83300690712bd7ad03a1442ab3d8f45</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520--59931f2b4e41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters have decisively rejected a proposal to begin the legal process toward Alberta's independence, dealing a major blow to a movement driven largely by economic grievances.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP seriously hurt in suspected car attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e034d8a67f563946a15987597a96b060f8f693a4176e901366d4180219294810</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660--8ec3224c2b82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Helen Haines, an independent federal lawmaker, suffered severe injuries in what Australia's prime minister has called a deliberate attack by a man in a car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b37a52bab194f6232d5aee9842eb9fc90732265bc37f849d6241faf20f990f4b</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta votes on holding independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3576b185a6d39fc721d550601d7b89d5fe0d22677820517a6ae2925dfa08c55e</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283--4cfaa44e1aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada's oil-rich western province of Alberta is not deemed likely to vote in favor of a real breakaway plebiscite. Nevertheless the separatist movement hopes to gain leverage over Mark Carney's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
